@startuml activity-note-signature-cost
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because the experiment is a chain whose ORDER is part of its validity: every registration is
'' written into the ledger before the run it judges, and each result either confirms a design or opens the question
'' the next registration answers. Activity swimlanes show who owns each step (the ledger, the instruments, the designs
'' under test), the `if` steps show which outcome led where, the formulas render as LaTeX, and the SVG renders
'' byte-reproducibly (README §4).
'' Lanes and fills, from the shared palette: tan = the append-only ledger, fixed before the runs it judges (the files
'' on disk of docs/scientific/data/14); slate = the Node instruments (the benchmark under taskset, the census, E1 and
'' E3); orange = the designs under test, the "model orange" of the pure vinary.slides.* libraries; red = a refutation
'' or a rejection; green = held, or adopted.
!include _vv-theme.iuml
!pragma useVerticalIf on

title H-PAIRWORK and its fix: nine registrations, each written before the run it judges (scientific/14 §2)

|#EEEBE8|the ledger (PREREGISTRATION.txt)|
start
