|#F5EAE0|the designs under test (vinary.slides.notes)|
:F written; E1 with five negative controls, all killed;  <<IR_TINT>>
|#E4E8F1|the instruments (scripts/bench-note-signature.cjs, the census, E1, E3)|
:E2: 38 830 census pairs, E3: 155 decks — no disagreement.
The bench: A(4096) 5.35 ms, C 48.6 ms (≤ 50, > 16);  <<MAIN_TINT>>
|#EEEBE8|the ledger (PREREGISTRATION.txt)|
:**3 · H-FLOOD, H-FAR**: a design review attacks F's time.
Can crafted cells share one bucket of V8's number hash?
Can far cells fall back to string keys?;  <<FS_TINT>>
|#E4E8F1|the instruments (scripts/bench-note-signature.cjs, the census, E1, E3)|
:flood <latex>77.6\times</latex> its random control (2.33 s); far <latex>7.66\times</latex>;  <<MAIN_TINT>>
:**F rejected** for the hostile case;  <<ERROR_TINT>>
|#EEEBE8|the ledger (PREREGISTRATION.txt)|
:**4 · design F′**: its own table, hashed at random per call,
amended BEFORE it is written: simple tabulation, not a
linear family (3-independent; Chernoff-type loads);  <<FS_TINT>>
|#F5EAE0|the designs under test (vinary.slides.notes)|
:F′ written; E1 extended, 11 controls killed; E2, E3 identical;  <<IR_TINT>>
|#E4E8F1|the instruments (scripts/bench-note-signature.cjs, the census, E1, E3)|
:at the match cap 65 536, C 34.7 ms > 16: the rule lowers
